            "review_text": "DaTripper2014\nSaskatoon, Canada65 contributions\n2\nSo delicious!!\nFeb 2019 • Couples\nNOTE: THE ADDRESS FOR THIS TRIPADVISOR LISTING IS INCORRECT.\n\nBun Rieu Cua is located in Hanoi Old Quarter at 11 Hang Bac. One of GoogleMaps addresses is correct - it was literally a few doors over (maybe 50 metres) from the Oriental Central Hotel.\n\nNow on to the review.\n\nWe were brought here as part of a street food tour. What a discovery! Only one dish - that the lady cooks up every day and many locals stream by to eat a bowl, sitting at small plastic chair either along inside counter or outside. Absolutely delicious tomato based clear broth soup with rice noodles. Tofu, Hanoi sausage and meat for protein (second time we asked for only the tofu). Greens on the side to add in to your soup. Large bowl is filling and was only 30,000 VND. (We shared both times we went as we were also trying other food elsewhere).\n\nSo good we came back to Bun Rieu Cua the next day on our own for another bowl! Breakfast, lunch or dinner - your choice.\nRead more\nWritten February 17, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
